      "problem": "If $\\frac{1}{7}x-5=-4,$ then $x=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $5$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7}x-5 & =-4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}x-5+5 & =-4+5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}x+0 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, multiplying both sides by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7}x & =1 \\\\ \\cancel{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cancel{7}}x & =7\\cdot 1 \\\\ x & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$",
